{
 "_anchor": "record_ref carries an ANCHOR the resolver opens at ruled_at: #class-X for ARM 4 (this record rules BY CLASS -- 'the reason IS the record'), #rows-N,M for ARM 1 (that record rules row by row). An entry whose anchor is absent from the record at its own ruled_at is an ORPHAN. RESIDUAL: class anchoring is COARSER than row anchoring -- it proves a ruling section covering this class exists at a real commit, not that this exact arm was itemised. Closing that needs the record to itemise 24 rows, which is an ADJUDICATION act, not the gate's.",
 "_class_D": "DEFERRED BY LANDED DESIGN, never suppressed -- printed every run with its reversal trigger (R2-2's landing makes corroborated + superseded_by the desired expressible state) so it returns by construction rather than by anyone remembering.",
 "_dead_arms": "An entry whose arm no longer exists carries arm_digest ARM_ABSENT + arm_absent_at. It suppresses nothing (no live row can key to it) and cannot be revived silently.",
 "_generated": "DERIVED from ARM 4's own output at the adjudicated tip -- never hand-listed, so it cannot drift from the arm it disposes.",
 "_key": "record_type|discriminant|field|value-set  -- THE VALUE SET IS PART OF THE ARM'S IDENTITY. A (record_type, discriminant, field) TRIPLE IS NOT UNIQUE: entity_binding.binding_basis and identity_relation.claim_origin each carry TWO arms requiring evidence_refs on DIFFERENT value sets, and a triple key silently collapsed 20 rows to 18 -- suppressing an arm nobody ruled on. Found by generating the sidecar, not by designing it.",
 "_lapse": "If a (record_type, discriminant, field) exists here but with a DIFFERENT value set, the suppression LAPSES and the row is reported RE-ADJUDICATION REQUIRED, naming both sets. A ruling about a 4-value enum does not survive it becoming 5. An arm absent entirely is reported NEW. Neither is ever silently suppressed.",
 "_link": "R3-CVO-2: every entry carries record_ref + ruled_at + arm_digest. An entry missing any is an ORPHAN -> IGNORED -> the row prints NEW + WARN (fail-open-to-NEW, never to suppressed). A digest that no longer matches the live arm is STALE -> RE-ADJUDICATION.",
 "_record": "org/standards/isck/ARM4_ADJUDICATION.md",
 "_ruled_by": "1.0.0_SA_CTO~X (77047 concur; rulings in ARM4_ADJUDICATION.md)",
